          "body": "Sean, 2026-10-14: \"story page only\". Nothing here deploys; Sean deploys.\n\n## Where it goes: trustshell.dev `/trust-medical` (rewritten in place)\n**Searched (origin default branches):**\n- **trustshell** (trustshell.dev): `/vision` lists every Trust* surface, and `/trust-medical` already exists (#531, \"a door, not a trial\"), linked from `/vision`, the footer and the sitemap. It hosts `/check`, `/how-verification` and `/passport/*`, the HAL and zkRepID pages a stranger reads.\n- **trustmarket** (private; landing branch has `app/vision`): no medical content, and the repo is private.\n- **hyperdag-protocol**: a protocol repo with markdown, and only two passing mentions of the word \"health\".\n- **hyperdag-landing** (hyperdag.org, last push 08-21), **repid**, **trustrepid**, **aitrinitysymphony-landing**, **trustmarketing**: no vision or medical page.\n\n**Chosen: trustshell.dev.** It is where a stranger reading about TrustShell, HAL and zkRepID already is, and it already routes to `/trust-medical`. Rewriting that page avoids a second TrustMedical page.\n\n## The page\n- **Label.** `Vision — not built yet` is in the `<title>`, the eyebrow and the badge.\n- **Disclaimer, near the top.** \"Not a medical product. It does not exist yet. Nothing here is medical advice. This page has no form and collects nothing.\"\n- **Five ideas, plain language**, from `ZKP_ARCHITECTURE_INVARIANTS.md`:\n  - one identity with a separate consent proof per study (scoped nullifier);\n  - one rulebook for consent (the same consent/owner-policy engine as agent ownership);\n  - RepID deciding which research agents may come near a study;\n  - claims about a study get checked (HAL grounding);\n  - health data in its own database, never the agent network's (the data-plane isolation rule).\n- **What exists today**, each item linked:\n  - `/check`: two model families, a receipt, and Not checked never counts as a pass;\n  - `/passport/trinity-sophia`: a zero-knowledge range proof over RepID. Today that proof shows the score rather than hiding it, which matches the live passport [V];\n  - `/how-verification`.\n- **What does not exist**, named piece by piece.\n- About 470 words, existing components only, no new dependency.\n\n## Guard: `tests/trust-medical-page.test.ts` (5 tests)\n- The label is in the title, eyebrow and badge, and the disclaimer is word for word.\n- No `form`, `input`, `textarea`, `select`, `button` or client-side state.\n- None of: HIPAA, GDPR, compliance, clinical, diagnosis, treatment, medical advice outside the negation, customer, partner, pilot, launch, enrol, secure, private, quarter or any year.\n- Broken on purpose, each turns it red: label removed, \"HIPAA compliant\" added, a form added.\n\nFull local unit run: same Windows ENV failures as on main, plus two regex-timing suites that pass when rerun alone. CI decides.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
